# escalation-furnish.rq — a region the reader could not read, stated as the decision it is.
#
# why-escalated.rq answers "why was this region escalated?"; this answers the other half —
# what that escalation OBLIGES. A recorded escalation verdict becomes the three predicates
# dec:EscalationShape reads (dec:constrainedBy, dec:withinScope, dec:escalatedTo) plus the
# human-addressed dec:ExpansionRequest it escalates to. Without this the shape has 769 focus
# nodes and binds zero rows: it targets dec:DecisionHolon but nothing in the pipeline ever
# wrote the severity/scope pair its body joins on (residue R87).
#
# GATE (CLAUDE.md §8): AXIOM, derivation form. Open world, evidence-positive, idempotent. It
# decides nothing — the reading judgement was already made and recorded at the call site; this
# states its consequence.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LICENCE — why a derivation may carry VOCABULARY triples into a document's data graph.
#
# dec:EscalationShape's sh:sparql body reads five triples, of which three are vocabulary:
# `?scope dec:maxSeverity ?ceil`, `?sev risk:order ?so`, `?ceil risk:order ?co`. A SHACL
# data graph that lacks them cannot satisfy the shape, so the derivation carries exactly
# those three out with the data it furnishes.
#
# The licence is BOUNDED, and the boundary is what makes it a licence rather than a merge:
#   * bounded to the triples that shape's body reads FROM THE TERMS THIS QUERY NAMES —
#     not "the vocabulary", not risk.ttl, not every risk:Severity's ordinal;
#   * carried inside the CONSTRUCT template, so CONSTRUCT semantics enforce the boundary for
#     free: no escalation matched => empty output => ZERO vocabulary triples in the document.
#
# What this licence is NOT: permission to merge risk.ttl into a data graph (that asserts the
# whole file unconditionally on every document, escalating or not), and not a precedent for
# any shape that would merely find a vocabulary triple convenient. Pinned by the tests at
# tests/etkl/test_escalation_furnish.py — T2.4 fails if the carry grows OR shrinks.
#
# The ordinals are BOUND from risk.ttl below, never written as literals here. That is the
# whole difference from restating the scale in this file, and T2.3 is the property that
# proves it: retune risk:Breach's ordinal in the vocabulary graph and the carried triple
# follows it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SUPERSESSION GUARD. Section repair adopts a pass-2 re-read of a band and links the two
# verdict decisions with dec:supersedes, so a pass-1 verdict that chose "escalated" can be a
# WITHDRAWN reading. Furnishing it would escalate to a human a matter a later reading already
# resolved. MEASURED 2026-08-15: all 4 of cbh-stem-2026-08-03's decisions that chose
# "escalated" carry an incoming dec:supersedes edge, which is why that document's region
# verdicts show zero escalated. The FILTER NOT EXISTS is a HOLON-SCOPED closed-world guard
# (?d is bound by the pattern above it, so the negation is scoped to that one decision) —
# it selects between two PRESENT readings and never derives a fact from absence. Same
# construct and same classification as effective-chain.rq, whose header states the rule.
#   SITE CONSTRAINT this places on the caller: run the derivation AFTER section repair has
#   linked its dec:supersedes edges. Run before, and the guard is vacuous.
#   SINGLE-HOP, as in effective-chain.rq: one dec:supersedes edge is enough to withdraw a
#   reading, so no transitive walk is needed here — a chain's every non-final link carries an
#   incoming edge and is excluded on its own account.
#
# ?req is a FUNCTION of ?d (not a blank node, not minted fresh), so the derivation is a pure
# function of the graph and running it twice adds nothing: idempotence is structural rather
# than asserted. A blank node would also be safe against the membrane (it skolemizes the
# payload, membrane.py:318) but dec:EscalationShape carries sh:sparql and R88's pin history
# is about exactly that; a stable IRI needs no engine caveat.
PREFIX dec:  <https://w3id.org/iladub/dec#>
PREFIX etkl: <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#>
PREFIX risk: <https://w3id.org/iladub/risk#>
PREFIX rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
CONSTRUCT {
  ?d   dec:constrainedBy risk:Breach ;
       dec:withinScope   etkl:readerScope ;
       dec:escalatedTo   ?req .
  ?req rdf:type          dec:ExpansionRequest ;
       dec:regarding     ?r ;
       dec:condition     ?why .
  # the three carried vocabulary triples — see LICENCE above
  etkl:readerScope dec:maxSeverity ?ceil .
  risk:Breach      risk:order      ?so .
  ?ceil            risk:order      ?co .
}
WHERE {
  ?d a dec:DecisionHolon ;
     dec:chosen ?o ;
     dec:rationale ?why .
  # THE LABEL, never the option URI's suffix: `{d}-opt-{slug}` is decisionlog.py's private
  # spelling (:59) and no query may depend on it. Nor the call site — 17 sites record a
  # verdict and not all of them can choose "escalated"; the chosen option is the evidence.
  ?o rdfs:label "escalated" .
  # REQUIRED, never OPTIONAL: this join is invariant 5's guard. A decision carrying no
  # dec:regarding derives NOTHING AT ALL, rather than a request with no subject matter.
  # Live rather than vacuous — datagrid.py mints decision holons and emits no dec:regarding.
  ?d dec:regarding ?r .
  # withdrawn readings — see SUPERSESSION GUARD above
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?later dec:supersedes ?d }
  # bound from the vocabulary graph, never written
  risk:Breach risk:order ?so .
  etkl:readerScope dec:maxSeverity ?ceil .
  ?ceil risk:order ?co .
  FILTER (?so > ?co)
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR(?d), "-expansion")) AS ?req)
}
